abstract: >-
  A beginner friendly lesson on data visualization and map design for social
  scientists. It covers why and how to visualize data honestly, a checklist
  for planning maps, the fundamentals of cartographic design (map elements,
  color schemes, projections, thematic map types, normalization and
  classification), making a first map in QGIS, and designing accessible maps
  for people with color vision deficiency. Python notebooks in Google Colab
  complement the QGIS exercises.
